message:
I found a potential issue in `md_analyze_table_alignment`. The function has:
```c
while(n_align > 0) {
    int index = 0;
    while(CH(off) != _T('-'))
        off++;
    ...
}
```

The `while(CH(off) != _T('-'))` loop reads `CH(off)` without checking if `off < end`. If the table underline doesn't have enough `-` characters, this could read past the end of the input buffer. But wait, `CH(off)` reads from `ctx->text` which is the input buffer. If `off` goes past `ctx->size`, it reads out of bounds.

But actually, looking at the `md_is_table_underline` function, it should validate the underline format first. Let me look at that.

<｜｜DSML｜｜ode>

<｜｜DSML｜｜function=execute_bash>
<parameter=command>cd /workspace && sed -n '5172,5260p' repo-vul/src-vul/md4c/src/md4c.c</parameter>
</｜｜DSML｜｜function>

